\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid15926043\charrsid15926043  What is meant by term \'93Color shows relationships\'94 with respect to misuse of colors in visual interface? [2]
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6492237 {\b\f0\fs26\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6492237 The use of color
\par }{\f0\fs23\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6492237 Ergonomics has a close relationship to human psychology in that it is also concerned with
\par the perceptual limitations of humans. For example, the use of color in displays is an
\par ergonomics issue. The human visual system has some limitations with regard to color,
\par including the number of colors that are distinguishable and the relatively low blue acuity.
\par Color used in display should be as distinct as possible and the distinction should not be
\par affected by changes in contrast. The colors used should also correspond to common
\par conventions and user expectation. However, we should remember that color conventions
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6492237 {\f0\fs23\cf0\ulc0\insrsid6492237 are culturally determined.}{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid15926043\charrsid15926043 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid15926043\charrsid15926043     }{\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid15926043\charrsid15926043 
